AB  - In the context of deep integration of intelligent knowledge management technology into educational innovation, the traditional BOPPPS teaching model lacks corresponding capabilities and exhibits deficiencies in knowledge updat- ing, knowledge organization, personalized adaptation, and dynamic feedback. This paper proposes a deep integration of Knowledge-Augmented Generation (KAG) technology with the BOPPPS teaching model, presenting a three- dimensional collaborative teaching framework driven by knowledge graphs, goal-oriented personalized adaptation, and intelligent interactive feedback. While preserving the structured advantages of BOPPPS, this framework incor- porates the generative capabilities of large language models and knowledge graph technology to enhance personalized adaptation of teaching objectives, interactive feedback during the learning process, and knowledge system updating and augmentation. The teaching model proposed in this research is expected to improve the practical effectiveness of the BOPPPS teaching model, students’ innovative problem-solving abilities, and interdisciplinary thinking levels, while providing reference for implementing intelligent knowledge management technology in educational settings.
